      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s northern border follows the Farmington River, while Talcott Mountain on the west forms part of the Metacomet Ridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomfield%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bloomfield is home to the historic Old Farm School, a restored 1796 building that once served as a community schoolhouse.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
